      "side": 1,
      "message": "This feels like a step in the wrong direction. We\u0027ve been doing a lot of work to make our interfaces safe by spanifying them. Removing spans and going back to pointer + count seems wrong.\n\nThe chromium ban is for general chromium use, but if you\u0027re interfacing with third_party code, is span still banned? Is there no way to go from std::span to base::span? I think this is a question that should be brought up to the cxx list before removing span and making our interfaces less safe.",
      "revId": "d6edbbd072c3eae2e80bd84de498b1b837293dfe",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
