      "writtenOn": "2026-04-08T17:19:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed.\n\n`base::span` converts implicitly to `std::span` but if you want to go the other way I think you have to do it explicitly. That doesn\u0027t make a difference though, we would have to write std::span in chromium anyway this is a method overload (so it has to have the same type as the interface it\u0027s overloading).\n\nThere must be a way to get an exception / silence the warning about using std::span in this one spot. Maybe it\u0027s just a presubmit warning and can be ignored? Maybe there\u0027s a NOLINT directive for it? I don\u0027t remember.",
